    {
      "id": "ad3c4e7e-52e6-5e1d-a745-53489898895e",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -540,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## WF-00 Dispatcher & Scheduler\n**Durable timers + transactional outbox.** Every status change writes its follow-up into `ops.scheduled_actions` in the same database transaction; reminders and expiries are rows with a future `run_at`.\n\n### How a run works\n1. Claim due rows with `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` (overlapping runs are safe).\n2. Route each action to its owning workflow (table in **Route by Action Type**).\n3. Record **DONE**, **SKIPPED** (state moved on) or **FAILED**.\n\n### Failures\n- FAILED is retried with exponential backoff (30 s up to 1 h).\n- After the last attempt the action lands in the error queue (WF-07, replayable).\n\n### Triggers\n- Every minute (safety net).\n- **Kick Webhook** `POST /webhook/ops/kick`: the backend calls it right after a person acts.\n- **When Kicked by Workflow**: intake and replays start it immediately.",
        "width": 680,
        "height": 520,
        "color": 4
      }
    }
  ],
